{
  "_comment": "Declarative vessel inventory for the substrate image. apply-inventory.sh reads this at boot (before systemd) to select which units run, so one image runs any SUBSET: a full local substrate, a minimal hub (store+control+api+transport), or a compute-only spoke. DEFAULT (no ENABLED_ROLES/ENABLED_VESSELS env) = every unit enabled, identical to today. Selection env: ENABLED_ROLES=comma,roles | ENABLED_VESSELS=comma,units (explicit, overrides roles) | DISABLED_VESSELS=comma,units (always off). Per-vessel fork remotes: repo_owner_default (or per-vessel repo_owner) + the `repo` field feed setup-git-push.sh / clone-vessel-repos so a fork can point vessels at its own GitHub org. NAMED PROFILE 'analysis-backend' (the minimum backend a white-labelled metabob-mcp client attaches to = discovery + concept-db + analysis-vessel + activity-api + store/identity/seed/infra deps) is not a role-group here because concept-db/analysis-vessel share the coarse 'compute' role; it is expressed as an explicit ENABLED_VESSELS list in scripts/substrate/deploy-analysis-backend.sh \u2014 keep that list in sync with the units below.",
  "repo_owner_default": "AviGopal",
  "branch_default": "dev",
  "roles": {
    "hub": [
      "store",
      "control",
      "api",
      "transport",
      "seed",
      "infra",
      "registry"
    ],
    "spoke": [
      "compute",
      "ui",
      "seed",
      "infra",
      "registry"
    ],
    "full": [
      "store",
      "control",
      "api",
      "compute",
      "ui",
      "transport",
      "seed",
      "infra",
      "autonomy",
      "registry"
    ]
  },
  "_profiles_comment": "Named per-container rosters as EXPLICIT unit lists. Roles are coarse — 'compute' names goal-host, development, light-dispatch, boredom, analysis, ribosome, relevance-sink, local-tools and the LLM resolvers together, so no role expression selects a subset of them. That is why ui-only-up.sh had to bypass roles with a hand-written ENABLED_VESSELS list. A profile is that list, named and kept next to the units it selects. PROFILE=<name> wins over ENABLED_VESSELS and ENABLED_ROLES; DISABLED_VESSELS still subtracts afterwards. human-surface-vessel is deliberately absent from surface_node: it is a manifest vessel, which apply-inventory never selects or masks, and vessel-ctl installs it after readiness. CAVEAT (the reason a profile is not yet a guarantee): apply-inventory can only govern units this file names, so a shipped unit absent from `vessels` below runs regardless of the profile — that is how a UI-only box ends up running LLM resolvers. See the ungoverned-units warning apply-inventory emits at boot.",
  "profiles": {
    "compute_node": [
      "discovery-vessel.service",
      "goal-host-vessel.service",
      "development-vessel.service",
      "light-dispatch-vessel.service",
